# Manual chapter 23, "Egress through a provider" and "Flow signatures".
#
# The same environment `examples/infoflow/governance.policy` labels, with the
# two grants that clear the doors REMOVED — no `grant provider fixture` and no
# `grant output result`. An ungranted principal sits at the bottom of both axes
# (public), so `examples/infoflow/agent-egress.whip` is refused twice: once for
# the turn context that reaches the model, once for the payload that reaches the
# invoker. Restore either grant and that half passes, which is the chapter's
# point: governance decides which models and which invokers are in the trust
# domain, and the author does not.
#
# It is a separate file rather than an edit to governance.policy because that
# policy is the one the infoflow examples pass under; making it fail would break
# the thing it demonstrates.

# The CRM holds customer PII. Only a party acting for Operator may read it, and
# only Operator-vouched data may be written into it.
grant file_store crm -> file:/srv/crm.db readable by Operator from Operator
